WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.834 line:0%
-Let's bring out Bari.
-(CHEERING)

00:00:02.368 --> 00:00:05.004
She's a staff editor and writer
for the opinion section
of<i> The New York Times,</i>

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:06.839
Bari Weiss is back with us.

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:09.909
-(CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)
-BILL: Hey, you.

00:00:10.943 --> 00:00:13.079
-How are you?
-I'm good, how are you?

00:00:13.212 --> 00:00:15.315
-Weren't you just here?
-Yeah, just here.

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:16.949
You must have done so good

00:00:17.082 --> 00:00:18.751
-you came back so quickly.
-(BARI CHUCKLES)

00:00:18.951 --> 00:00:20.986
Uh, but you did do good,
everybody loved you...

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.857
-Thank you.
-...and also, you're sort of
on my side about a lot of issues

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:25.858
and by this point of the show,
I'm so argued out...

00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:27.693
-(BARI CHUCKLES)
-...I gotta have somebody
who agrees with me, so...

00:00:27.893 --> 00:00:29.695
-Okay, I'll pick up the flag.
-No, but I know-- We're--

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:32.231
We're both sort of fighting
the outrage machine, you know,

00:00:32.331 --> 00:00:34.033
the, uh, the professional
outrage people,

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:36.036
and let's just first get out
your, your--

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:38.871
'Cause I saw you got into
some hot water, for nothing!

00:00:39.038 --> 00:00:41.307
-I've got into a bunch
of hot water recently, so...
-Okay, but the--

00:00:41.507 --> 00:00:43.709
the-- the immigration-- It's
gotten to the point where, like,

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:45.712
I don't even know what the fuck
they're mad at anymore.

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:47.513
I used to at least go,
"Okay, I get it,

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:49.315
I understand, it's ridiculous,
but I get--"

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:50.983
Now, I don't even understand
what they're mad at.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:52.418
The tweet was what? You--

00:00:52.518 --> 00:00:54.120
-you were watching the Olympics?
-The tweet was--

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:55.855
Mirai Nagasu.

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:58.357
A, uh, person born
in California,

00:00:58.457 --> 00:01:00.393
-her parents are Japanese
immigrants...
-BILL: Okay.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:03.162
-...landed a historic
Triple Axel at the Olympics.
-BILL: Oh, right, yes.

00:01:03.262 --> 00:01:06.432
I tweeted out a video,
along with a lyric from<i> Hamilton</i>

00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:08.734
that said, "Immigrants,
they get the job done."

00:01:08.834 --> 00:01:11.604
Now, the actual lyric is,
"We", I got the lyric wrong--

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:14.274
-BILL: How dare you!
-And I was jumped upon.
Now, here's the thing--

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:17.076
-Oh, for fuck's sake.
-Anyone-- I despise xenophobia.

00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:19.278
-Anyone who reads my work...
-I despise-- Yes.

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:22.214
-...knows that I love immigrants
and the idea that--
-BILL: It's-- It's-- It's--

00:01:22.281 --> 00:01:25.084
-No, hold on. The idea
that I would in any way...
-(BILL CHUCKLES)

00:01:25.217 --> 00:01:27.687
...contribute to a culture
of hostility

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:30.223
towards minorities
and immigrants is horrible to me

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:32.925
and I feel awful
that anyone heard it that way.

00:01:33.059 --> 00:01:35.128
Wha-- What is-- What is--
What is your estimation

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:37.463
of why there's this fringe
on the left,

00:01:37.763 --> 00:01:39.532
that attacks people
like you and me,

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:41.567
who they must know
are not racist,

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:43.636
wha-- Is it just lazy?

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:46.205
That it's just too hard
to attack the real villains?

00:01:46.305 --> 00:01:48.173
-I think that a-- I--
-So you-- you fight...

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:50.576
-battles way behind enemy lines?
-I think-- I think, A,

00:01:50.676 --> 00:01:52.745
it's the narcissism
of small differences.

00:01:52.911 --> 00:01:55.215
Anyone that departs
from woke orthodoxy,

00:01:55.482 --> 00:01:57.983
-gets a lot more heat
in my opinion...
-Right.

00:01:58.083 --> 00:01:59.952
...than people
on the actual right.

00:02:00.152 --> 00:02:03.055
I also think that offence-taking
is being weaponized.

00:02:03.222 --> 00:02:05.358 line:0%
It is a root now
to political power.

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:06.859 line:0%
-BILL: Wow.
-Saying that, "I am offended"

00:02:06.959 --> 00:02:09.095 line:0%
-is a way of making someone
radioactive.
-BILL: Right.

00:02:09.261 --> 00:02:11.230 line:0%
It's a way
of smearing their reputation,

00:02:11.363 --> 00:02:12.865
of making them a liability,

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:14.567
because once you tar
someone

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:17.203
as a racist or a misogynist,
or a fascist, or...

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:19.071
-whatever the word
of the day is...
-BILL: Right.

00:02:19.271 --> 00:02:21.841
...um, you know, it's a way of
sort of taking them down a peg,

00:02:21.974 --> 00:02:23.375
and I'm really concerned...

00:02:23.542 --> 00:02:24.843
-Yeah.
-...not about, you know,

00:02:24.943 --> 00:02:27.880
people that have a public
platform like me or like you,

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:30.315
but the downstream effects
of these smearings,

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:32.552
because here's what happens
if you are someone

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:34.554
who wants to get in
into the public square,

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:36.422
and wants to say something
provocative

00:02:36.555 --> 00:02:38.624
and peep your head out
over the parapet.

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:41.760
You are not gonna do that,
you're gonna hesitate
from doing that

00:02:41.894 --> 00:02:43.696
if you know that
there's a mob awaiting you.

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:45.330
And you see what happens,
you know,

00:02:45.464 --> 00:02:47.233
to very, very, prominent people,

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:49.668
for-- for saying sort of
the smallest things.

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:51.571
-It-- Can I say one more thing?
-BILL: Yeah, Matt Damon.

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:53.272
-Yeah, no, please. You know...
-Yeah, Matt Damon, I mean, so--

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:55.141
...just, husbanditis,
I call it.

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:57.343
-So-- Well...
-I'm-- I'm just shutting up.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.412
-(LAUGHTER)
-I really-- I've been revisiting

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:02.081
the-- the Philip Roth book,
<i> The Human Stain,</i> okay?

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:04.283
<i> The Human Stain,</i>
two sentences on it,

00:03:04.484 --> 00:03:07.153
it's about a classicist,
at a small liberal arts school,

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:09.622
who uses the word "spooks,"
meaning ghosts,

00:03:09.789 --> 00:03:10.823
-he means it literally.
-BILL: Right.

00:03:10.956 --> 00:03:12.592
It's taken as a racist slur,

00:03:12.758 --> 00:03:14.960
and what happens to him
is personal ruin.

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:17.463
Now, the irony of this
is he, himself,

00:03:17.563 --> 00:03:20.166
is a light-skinned black man
who's passing as a Jew.

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:23.569
I'm reminded of this because
we sort of live in the age

00:03:23.802 --> 00:03:25.071
of the digital stain.

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:26.739
-What people are trying to do...
-BILL: Hmm.

00:03:26.872 --> 00:03:29.275
is to take even the most
well-intentioned,

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:30.910
and anodyne comment

00:03:31.043 --> 00:03:32.445
intentionally twerk it,

00:03:32.611 --> 00:03:33.579
and then throw it out

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:35.581
through the echo-chamber
of social media,

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:37.983
in order to ruin
people's reputations.

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:40.619
And I think it's very strange
that we're liv--

00:03:40.719 --> 00:03:43.623
We're the most privileged people
in human history, objectively.

00:03:43.789 --> 00:03:46.392
And yet people are spending
all of their time on Earth,

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:48.227
hurling pixels at one another.

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:50.829
-Right-- (CHUCKLES)
-I find it a very, very strange
use of people's time.

00:03:50.896 --> 00:03:54.467
-Well, it-- I mean,
it's so well said, all of it.
-(CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)

00:03:56.335 --> 00:03:57.337
And...

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:01.207
I also think people are
schizophrenic,

00:04:01.374 --> 00:04:04.610
they're the real people
who talk in private
with their friends

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:06.178
and how they conduct themselves

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:07.613
-in a setting that's not--
-Yeah.

00:04:07.746 --> 00:04:08.981
And then, there's like the--

00:04:09.081 --> 00:04:11.817
Because everybody is
on social media,
that's like their avatar.

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:14.920
And that person is
super politically correct...

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:16.522
-Right.
-...about everything.

00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:18.991
It's like everybody have
their own publicist.

00:04:19.392 --> 00:04:21.760
-(CHUCKLES) Right.
-Who's them on social media,

00:04:21.927 --> 00:04:23.763
-and-- and it's making me crazy.
-But also-- But also

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:25.664
it's the opposite.
Also in real life

00:04:25.797 --> 00:04:27.332
-people are... civilized.
-BILL: Right.

00:04:27.466 --> 00:04:29.635
People say,
"I'm sorry, I didn't mean that,

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:30.937
-I-- It's a misunderstanding."
-BILL: Right.

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:34.273
But on social media,
they're acting like Torquemadas.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:35.541
-I mean, it's bizarre.
-Right.

